{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L53"},"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertices","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Vertices.Index == Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; on "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, with no hashing, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}]},{"text":" In addition to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":"’s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a vertex with key ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the members of the same name without the label, for that vertex.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order; ","type":"text"},{"code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the endpoints’ keys.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex’s key is now "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"; otherwise it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, trapping on any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", returning the removed instance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":", then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"text":" for each vertex in order, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" for each pair","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in order: the same graph, and the same position for each pair.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key density.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", plus O(1) per live vertex: the memory of the representation’s own page","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span can exceed the vertex count: removals leave holes, and a decoded graph may start at any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position (its decoder bounds the span at ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × vertexCount + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages). Keys before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smallest live key cost nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key rows."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not requirements."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" differs in its return type: ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple, returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new position, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. So generic code inserts an edge by key, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hooks are underscored because they are for wrappers inside the library: callers use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representations’ own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"type":"text","text":" members, which take vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"required":true,"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Vertices","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(edge:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledir